EDITS = {'CHANGELOG.md': [('lines 1-2', '# Changelog\n\n', '# Changelog\n\n## [0.66.0] - Delco\'s asphalt at a weathered road\'s albedo\n\nThe walker, 2026-10-30, of the game\'s vertical slice: "keep getting us closer to that amazing vertical slice look".\n\n### Changed\n- **`asphalt_delco`\'s base colours** #33322f / #3a3936 / #2c2b28 -> #52514d / #5a5955 / #4a4945. Minted at 0.30.0\n  and never retuned for brightness, the pack\'s albedo map measured 0.035 linear -- darker than fresh asphalt (about\n  0.05-0.10) and a third of a weathered road\'s (0.10-0.20) -- and at Blue Hour the slice\'s avenue read as a black\n  band under every street view. The new map is 0.095 linear. Re-baked on the slice\'s walk copy with the map swapped\n  in (the factory\'s `docs/findings/sodium_pools/`): ave_east 48.9 -> 57.0 of 255, the gas forecourt 61.6 -> 72.1, and\n  the cracks and aggregate read inside each sodium pool. A map: no draw moves. `asphalt_street`, an older grammar no\n  Delco theme draws, is unchanged -- nothing has seen it on a level.\n- **`tools/art_standard_baseline.json` re-snapshotted**, the ceremony the art standard asks for a deliberate\n  regression: `asphalt_delco` brighter shows more of its own grain -- value_range 0.118 -> 0.204 and hf_energy 0.033\n  -> 0.060, chroma 0.006 -> 0.009 -- all inside the environment budget (value_range 0.500, chroma 0.030). The\n  snapshot also gains rows for three grammars added since the last (brick_brown_delco, brick_orange_delco,\n  chain_link_galvanized), which the budget judged and judges either way.\n\nTests: tests/test_asphalt_albedo.py (fails on 0.65.0).\n\n')], 'VERSION': [('lines 1-1', 'Pixelcoat 0.65.0', 'Pixelcoat 0.66.0')], 'pixelcoat/version.py': [('lines 33-33', '_FALLBACK = "0.65.0"\n', '_FALLBACK = "0.66.0"\n')], 'profiles/materials/asphalt_delco.json': [('lines 5-7', '    "#33322f",\n    "#3a3936",\n    "#2c2b28"\n', '    "#52514d",\n    "#5a5955",\n    "#4a4945"\n'), ('lines 53-53', '  "notes": "Aggregate at 150 cells on a 3 m tile is 2 cm of stone, which is what asphalt is. REFUTED ON THE WAY: the cell mosaic the walker kept seeing was read as the MESO band and it is not -- a before/after render (2026-09-13) showed the pattern unchanged when meso went from 22 cells to 150, because the cells are the `edges` layer, a 5-to-6-cell Worley crack network at 0.25 strength on a 3 m tile: 50 cm cracks in a grid, which is crazy paving. Edges are now 3 cells at 0.965 threshold, which is a few long cracks, and the aggregate does the rest. CORRECTED after cold run 9041: the crack layer is a closed tessellation, so the \'few long cracks\' the retune claimed were a honeycomb at every threshold. sparsity 0.3 breaks it. WET VARIANT: asphalt is impermeable, so rain sits on it rather than into it and the whole surface goes; amount 0.9 leaves the crowns of the aggregate reading dry, which is what stops a wet road looking like a poured one. Response from the concrete preset.",\n', '  "notes": "ALBEDO (0.66.0): the base colours were minted at #33322f / #3a3936 / #2c2b28 and the pack\'s albedo map measured 0.035 linear -- darker than fresh asphalt (about 0.05-0.10) and a third of a weathered road\'s (0.10-0.20). At Blue Hour the vertical slice\'s avenue read as a black band under every street view and its sodium pools found nothing to light. #52514d / #5a5955 / #4a4945 mint a map at 0.095 linear; re-baked on the slice (the factory\'s docs/findings/sodium_pools/), the cracks and aggregate read inside each pool. Aggregate at 150 cells on a 3 m tile is 2 cm of stone, which is what asphalt is. REFUTED ON THE WAY: the cell mosaic the walker kept seeing was read as the MESO band and it is not -- a before/after render (2026-09-13) showed the pattern unchanged when meso went from 22 cells to 150, because the cells are the `edges` layer, a 5-to-6-cell Worley crack network at 0.25 strength on a 3 m tile: 50 cm cracks in a grid, which is crazy paving. Edges are now 3 cells at 0.965 threshold, which is a few long cracks, and the aggregate does the rest. CORRECTED after cold run 9041: the crack layer is a closed tessellation, so the \'few long cracks\' the retune claimed were a honeycomb at every threshold. sparsity 0.3 breaks it. WET VARIANT: asphalt is impermeable, so rain sits on it rather than into it and the whole surface goes; amount 0.9 leaves the crowns of the aggregate reading dry, which is what stops a wet road looking like a poured one. Response from the concrete preset.",\n')]}
